=== task: multi easy
title: True of inorder
prompt: Choose **every** statement that is true of the inorder list of any non-empty binary tree.
* The first node is the leftmost node :: Right. Go left from the root until there's no left child.
* The last node is the rightmost node :: Right. Go right from the root until there's no right child.
* The root comes after every value in its left subtree :: Right. The whole left subtree comes first.
* On a binary search tree, the values come out sorted :: Right. Smaller values are on the left at every node.
- The first node is always a leaf :: The leftmost node can have a right child, which comes straight after it.
- The root is always in the middle of the list :: Only when both subtrees are the same size.
hint: Which node has nothing to its left at all?
hint: Can the leftmost node have a child on its right?
right: Leftmost first, rightmost last, each root after its left subtree, and sorted values for a search tree.
wrong: The walk starts at the end of the leftmost path and ends at the end of the rightmost path. The leftmost node needn't be a leaf, and the root's position depends on the subtree sizes.

